Description: lightweight CLI download accelerator with URL range and list expansion
 Hyperflux is a lightweight command line download accelerator and a fork of
 Axel. It speeds up downloads by opening multiple connections to a server and
 fetching different parts of the file in parallel.
 .
 It also understands URL expansion: a single URL containing {a,b}, {N..M} or
 [N-M] patterns is expanded into separate downloads. The installed command is
 "flux".
